                <mxCell id="title" value="&lt;b style='font-size:20px;color:#0D47A1'&gt;Solenoid via Dual-MOSFET Trigger Module — ADD RELAY CH2 BOOT INTERLOCK (ECO-004 Rev H)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#555;font-size:12px'&gt;SIG on BCM 16/PR.05/T36 · D4184-class, trigger 3.3–20V · GOODRIG 12V 2A valve · 1N5408 flyback · 10kΩ gate pull-down · 3A fuse · &lt;b style='color:#B71C1C'&gt;NEW: 12V feed gated by Monk Makes Relay CH2 (T13 / BCM 27)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/span&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;fontColor=#333;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="330" y="18" width="840" height="52" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="fault_banner" value="&lt;b style='color:#FFFFFF;font-size:11px'&gt;⚠ 2026-07-14 ROOT CAUSE: the Jetson boot firmware actively DRIVES PR.05 (T36) HIGH during boot — no pull-down can win against a driven pin.&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#FFCDD2;font-size:9px'&gt;LED goes BRIGHT for the whole boot window until app.py claims PR.05 and drives it LOW. This is what cooked module #1 (linear-region heating → FETs failed short at 9Ω). Software cannot close this window → the module's 12V must be physically gated by Relay CH2, which only closes after app.py is in control.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#C62828;strokeColor=#B71C1C;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=4;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="330" y="74" width="550" height="70" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
