                        <mxPoint x="980" y="400" as="targetPoint"/>
                    </mxGeometry>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="wire_outn_l" value="&lt;b style='font-size:10px;color:#1565C0'&gt;★ OUT − → solenoid (−)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="876" y="404" width="160" height="18" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="gndbus" value="" style="rounded=1;fillColor=#212121;strokeColor=#616161;shadow=1;arcSize=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="600" width="1160" height="30" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="gndbusl" value="&lt;b style='color:#E0E0E0;font-size:12px'&gt;COMMON GND BUS — Jetson GND + 12V PSU GND + module GND (header GND &amp; DC IN −) + Wago #2 (pull-down)&lt;/b&gt;" style="text;html=1;align=center;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="604" width="1160" height="22" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="pd_callout" value="&lt;b style='color:#BF360C;font-size:12px'&gt;TWO LAYERS OF PROTECTION&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#5D4037;font-size:10px'&gt;&lt;b&gt;10kΩ pull-down (keep):&lt;/b&gt; pins SIG to 0V when PR.05 merely floats — covers app crash, reset, wire-off.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Relay CH2 interlock (NEW):&lt;/b&gt; covers the boot window, where the firmware actively DRIVES PR.05 HIGH and defeats the pull-down. CH2 is open until app.py claims PR.05 and drives it LOW, so the module has no 12V while boot firmware owns the pin. app.py energizes CH2 (BCM 27 HIGH) at startup and releases it on shutdown.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFF3E0;strokeColor=#BF360C;fontColor=#333;fontSize=10;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=12;spacingTop=8;" vertex="1" parent="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="900" y="70" width="330" height="140" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="steps" value="&lt;b style='font-size:13px;color:#6A1B9A'&gt;Step-by-step (Rev H): add the Relay CH2 boot interlock — 3 wires&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;0. EVERYTHING OFF:&lt;/b&gt; Jetson off, 12V adapter unplugged, solenoid spade connectors pulled off.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;1. Find CH2&lt;/b&gt; on the Monk Makes relay board that already runs the pump on CH1. Its &lt;b&gt;Vcc (T2, +5V)&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;b&gt;GND (T9)&lt;/b&gt; are already wired — nothing to add there.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;2. NEW wire:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;T13 → CH2 IN&lt;/b&gt;. (T13/BCM 27 is the pin that drove the old discrete MOSFET gate — it is free, and the software now drives it again for this interlock.)&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;3. MOVE the 12V feed:&lt;/b&gt; the wire that now runs &lt;b&gt;+12V bus → 3A fuse → module DC IN +&lt;/b&gt; — unscrew it from &lt;b&gt;DC IN +&lt;/b&gt; only and land that end on &lt;b&gt;CH2 COM&lt;/b&gt;. The fuse stays in this wire.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;4. NEW wire:&lt;/b&gt; &lt;b&gt;CH2 NO → module DC IN +&lt;/b&gt; screw.&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;5. Touch nothing else:&lt;/b&gt; SIG/Wago #1, 10k pull-down, Wago #2 GND, DC IN −, OUT±, and the 1N5408 flyback all stay exactly as they are.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b style='color:#1B5E20'&gt;Power-up verification (solenoid still DISCONNECTED):&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V1.&lt;/b&gt; Before power: &lt;b&gt;SIG → GND ≈ 4.7–10kΩ&lt;/b&gt; (pull-down intact — if OL, a leg popped out of a Wago; fix first). &lt;b&gt;CH2 COM ↔ NO = OL&lt;/b&gt; (relay open).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V2.&lt;/b&gt; 12V on, Jetson still OFF: module LED &lt;b&gt;OFF&lt;/b&gt;, &lt;b&gt;module DC IN+ → GND = 0V&lt;/b&gt; (relay is open, module unpowered).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V3.&lt;/b&gt; Boot the Jetson: module LED must stay &lt;b&gt;OFF the entire boot&lt;/b&gt; — this is the interlock working (PR.05 goes HIGH but the module has no 12V). When app.py starts you'll hear the &lt;b&gt;CH2 relay click&lt;/b&gt;, then DC IN+ → GND = 12V and the LED stays off (SIG driven 0V).&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;V4.&lt;/b&gt; Dashboard click test: LED flashes, &lt;b&gt;OUT+ ↔ OUT−&lt;/b&gt; switches 12V↔0V. Only now power off and reconnect the solenoid.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#5D4037'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Software (already in hardware.py):&lt;/b&gt; PADCTL 0xD030 re-added for PY.00; RelayController claims PR.05 LOW first, then energizes CH2 (BCM 27 HIGH via libgpiod). Cleanup drops CH2 before releasing SIG. Status field: solenoid_12v.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style='color:#5D4037'&gt;&lt;b&gt;Recommended (commercial robustness):&lt;/b&gt; give the Jetson its own supply, separate from the solenoid 12V — a valve/driver fault must never brown out the flight computer.&lt;/span&gt;" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#F3E5F5;strokeColor=#8E24AA;fontColor=#333;fontSize=11;strokeWidth=2;align=left;spacingLeft=14;spacingRight=14;spacingTop=10;spacingBottom=10;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="60" y="650" width="1160" height="400" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="2" value="" style="shape=image;verticalLabelPosition=bottom;labelBackgroundColor=default;verticalAlign=top;aspect=fixed;imageAspect=0;image=http://www.haoyuelectronics.com/Attachment/MOSFET-Trigger-Switch-Module/MOSFET-Trigger-Switch-Module-7.jpg;" parent="1" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry x="1240" y="150" width="220" height="182" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
</mxfile>